## Structural map engine

**Location:** `internal/mapengine/` (Go package `mapengine`)

- `types.go` — engine types, options, and the routing/dispatch logic
- `goast.go` — `GoASTMapper`, built on `go/ast` for Go files
- `treesitter.go` — `TreeSitterMapper`, built on [gotreesitter](https://github.com/odvcencio/gotreesitter)
- `regex.go` (+ `regex_test.go`) — `RegexMapper`, the universal fallback
- `types.go` also defines the `Mapper` interface (`Map(path, content, opts) (Result, error)`), `Result`, `Symbol`, `Options`, `Engine`/`Level`/`Kind` enums, plus helpers `buildResultFromSymbols`, `kindSortRank`, `symbolKey`.

## Parser engine selection per file

Selection happens in `mapengine.Map` and `mapAuto` in `internal/mapengine/types.go` (lines ~125–159):

```go
func Map(path string, content []byte, opts Options) (Result, error) {
    switch opts.Engine {
    case EngineRegex:      return RegexMapper{}.Map(path, content, opts)
    case EngineTreeSitter: return mapTreeSitterWithFallback(path, content, opts, true)
    case EngineAuto:       return mapAuto(path, content, opts)
    default: /* unknown engine string → regex fallback with warning */
    }
}

func mapAuto(path string, content []byte, opts Options) (Result, error) {
    switch strings.ToLower(filepath.Ext(path)) {
    case ".go":
        // GoASTMapper; on error, falls back to RegexMapper (Fallback=true)
    case ".ts", ".tsx", ".js", ".jsx", ".py", ".rs":
        // TreeSitterMapper via mapTreeSitterWithFallback; on error/unsupported, falls back to regex
    default:
        return RegexMapper{}.Map(path, content, opts)
    }
}
```

So under the default `auto` engine: `.go` → `GoASTMapper` (go/ast, top-level declarations, generics preserved); `.ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/.py/.rs` → `TreeSitterMapper` (gotreesitter, reaches class/impl methods regex can't); everything else → `RegexMapper`. Any mapper error transparently falls back to regex with `Fallback: true` and a warning appended.

**CLI wiring:** `internal/cli/ghx.go:112,211` defines the `--map-engine` flag (default `"auto"`, choices `auto|regex|tree-sitter`), passed into `ghxlib.ReadOpts.MapEngine`. `internal/ghx/read.go:186-196` (function that handles `opts.Map` in `Read`) calls `mapengine.Map(path, content, mapengine.Options{Engine: mapengine.Engine(opts.MapEngine), ...})`, and stores the actual engine used back in `result.MapEngine` from `mapResult.Engine`.

**Not verified:** I did not read `treesitter.go`, `goast.go`, or `regex.go` bodies in full (only confirmed their existence and the mapper names referenced from `types.go`), nor did I check `docs/adr/` for the design rationale referenced in the README.

